-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision errors in calculating the projected scalar value can affect the merge decision, especially for very small $\epsilon$ [G].
-*   **Collinear Points:** If three consecutive knots are perfectly collinear, the vertical distance is $0.0$, so they will be merged if $\epsilon \ge 0.0$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The algorithm processes consecutive non-overlapping pairs [S1, unofficial]. The implementation above handles this by advancing the index [G]. Care must be taken to ensure that skipping a knot does not prevent a valid merge in the next step that involves the skipped knot's neighbor [G]. The iterative nature ensures convergence [S1, unofficial].
